  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rhiza Babuyile Primary Healthcare Programme.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks to provide Primary Healthcare Services nationally through mobile clinics. The project will provide national access to quality primary healthcare services for underserved urban, peri-urban and rural communities. Healthcare services include, sex education, family planning and the provision of contraceptives, curative care services, mother to childcare, dental health, HIV/AIDS treatment and care to pregnant mothers, hypertension and diabetes diagnosis and treatment, antenatal care, early detection of chronic illnesses and vision screening.

Target areas include, Gauteng: Diepsloot, Tembisa, Soweto and Orange Farm, Free State: Hani Park (Welkom), Limpopo: Waterberg Region, Mpumalanga: Middelburg and Mbombela, KwaZulu Natal: Umlazi, Louwsburg and Ntuzuma, Western Cape: Kayamandi, Philippi and Gugulethu, Eastern Cape: Mdantsani, Northwest Province: Rustenburg and Lichtenburg, Northern Cape: Kathu.</narrative>
  </description>
